<figure class="cache-figure" data-cache-burst>
 <p class="figure-title">Forty misses do not have to become forty source reads</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Requests in the burst <select data-kind><option value="same">All request the same key</option><option value="distinct">All request distinct keys</option></select></label><button data-complete>Complete source reads</button><button data-reset>Reset burst</button></div>
 <p class="figure-note">Redis is unavailable · four source permits and four initial tokens · at most sixteen waiters per shared fill</p>
 <div class="burst-requests" data-requests aria-hidden="true"></div>
 <p class="figure-note">S = starts a source read · W = waits for that shared read · × = refused</p>
 <div class="cache-stat-row local-reuse-stats"><div><strong data-source></strong><span>source reads started</span></div><div><strong data-active></strong><span>source reads still active</span></div><div><strong data-success></strong><span>successful responses completed</span></div><div><strong data-refused></strong><span>requests refused</span></div></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>A controlled burst model matching the lab’s admission cases: all forty requests arrive before admitted source work completes. Token refill is frozen for this experiment. The source replies successfully when released; a failure would change the admitted requests’ outcomes. These counts are not throughput measurements.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{burst}from'../../lib/caching/system-design.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cache-burst]').forEach(root=>{const kind=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-kind]')!,button=root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-complete]')!;let complete=false;const render=()=>{const s=burst(kind.value,complete);root.querySelector('[data-requests]')!.innerHTML=Array.from({length:40},(_,i)=>`<span class="${i<s.leaders?'leader':i<s.accepted?'follower':'refused'} ${complete&&i<s.accepted?'complete':''}">${i<s.leaders?'S':i<s.accepted?'W':'×'}</span>`).join('');for(const[k,v]of Object.entries({source:s.leaders,active:s.active,success:s.completed,refused:s.refused}))root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`)!.textContent=String(v);root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=`${s.leaders} source read${s.leaders===1?' serves':'s serve'} ${s.accepted} admitted requests; ${s.followers} share another request’s work. ${s.refused} are refused. ${complete?'The source work has finished and its permits are free.':'The admitted requests are waiting; permits remain occupied until the source work finishes.'}`;button.disabled=complete;};kind.onchange=()=>{complete=false;render();};button.onclick=()=>{complete=true;render();};root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.onclick=()=>{complete=false;render();};render();});
</script>
